    "body": "Calling `.addAbortCallback(yourCleanupFunction)` works just as well as using a symbol; arbitrary objects can have a method named `\"addAbortCallback\"`. There's no need to introduce a new symbol here.\r\n\r\nThe main reasons to use a symbol-based rather than string-based protocol are when this is a protocol that arbitrary objects might implement (like Iterator), or when you want to switch on the presence of the protocol (like Promise). Neither holds here.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
